---
# Wyoming-OpenAI Networking Configuration
## Configures container network connectivity via a systemd-container drop-in file.
## This allows the server maintainer to assign the container to specific networks
## (such as ai-network) to manage network isolation and connectivity.

variant: fcos
version: 1.6.0

storage:
  files:
    - path: /etc/containers/systemd/wyoming-openai/wyoming-openai.container.d/networking.conf
      overwrite: true
      contents:
        inline: |
          [Container]
          # Assign the container to the dedicated AI network
          Network=ai-network
      user:
        name: root
      group:
        name: root
      mode: 0644
